roving_review_count = 1` + `require_code_owner_reviews = true` per WP-SCP-020 020D2 spec. GitHub forbids PR authors from approving their own PRs. In single-operator mode with @jrnb2024 as the only maintainer AND only CODEOWNER, count=1 + codeowner=true locks the operator out of every PR; `enforce_admins=true` prevents `gh pr merge --admin` from bypassing. Updated to `count=0` + `codeowner_reviews=false` in single-operator mode. CODEOWNERS still serves as documentation of who SHOULD approve when a second maintainer arrives. Forward-looking discipline preserved: when a second maintainer onboards, flip count=1 + codeowner=true + non-author=true in one operation. Both corrections are landed in `scripts/configure-020d2-required-check.sh` (idempotent re-run reproduces the live state) + `docs/security/branch-protection.md` + WP-SCP-020 §8 risk row. The 2026-07-21 quarterly escalation review re-evaluates the personal-account shape | ACCEPTED | First-PR-through-enforcement is the operational test of the spec; the test surfaced two assumptions that didn't survive contact with GitHub's actual behaviour: (1) the bare context name from 020B(xi) was incomplete (didn't anticipate Actions' `<workflow> / <job>` rendering for reusable-workflow callers), and (2) \"self-approval is the only option\" in 020K's wording was operationally impossible (GitHub forbids PR self-review). Both corrections are operational closure of the spec gap; neither weakens the security posture. The 4-layer protection (signed commits + required check + no admin bypass + tag protection) remains intact. The review-count=0 acceptance is the explicit bus-factor-1 cost; review enforcement returns the moment a second maintainer joins. Identified by USER-GATE-A signoff PR #64's failed merge attempt 2026-04-30 |\n| D-034 | 2026-04-30 | Apply WP-SCP-020 slice 020F renovate-tag-protection (parallel ruleset to D-030's `v*` ruleset, targeting `refs/tags/renovate/v*`). Closes 020F R1 safety review CRIT-SAFE-001: `renovate